WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:08.060
- [Interviewer] All right, Maria.

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:10.663
Maria, where'd you grow up?
Where are you from originally?

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:13.070
- [Maria] Boyle Heights.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.960
- [Interviewer] So East LA?

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:15.800
- [Maria] Boyle Heights.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.420
East LA is a whole different ball game.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:18.253
- [Interviewer] Okay.

00:00:18.253 --> 00:00:19.760
And tell me about your family.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.637
Are both of your parents growing up?

00:00:21.637 --> 00:00:23.603
- I don't have my father,

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:26.600
but I have a great mom,

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.380
you know, like every other mother.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:33.380
You know, she struggled to make anything

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:35.310
possible for her kids, you know?

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.570
And my father was a great father,

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:42.010
but, you know, God took him so soon,

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:47.010
so I didn't have a father after
the age of five, you know?

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:51.320
So, you know, I kind
of grew up in the hood,

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:52.153
in the barrio.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.283
I learned the dope game,

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:58.650
and it was easy to, from there,

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:01.300
just to get money from guys.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.800
- [Interviewer] So you matured fast.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:06.262
- Yeah. It was way faster.

00:01:06.262 --> 00:01:07.095
- [Interviewer] 'Cause
you told me your age,

00:01:07.095 --> 00:01:09.090
and I have a hard time believing it.

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:09.923
How old are you?

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.450
- I don't wanna say my age.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.190
Okay. You told me a very young age.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:17.211
- I don't wanna say my age, you know?

00:01:17.211 --> 00:01:19.461
- [Interviewer] Understood.

00:01:20.619 --> 00:01:22.620
How would you describe your childhood?

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.690
- Kind of rough. You know what I'm saying?

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:27.740
But it was easy to fall into it on my end,

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.400
because, you know,
without a father figure,

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.190
trying to, you know,

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:35.950
help you, you know,
stay in the right place.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:39.090
You know, my mom taught me how,

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:42.520
you know, to do things a little different.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.590
So I liked it.

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:46.680
I'm not gonna sit here and lie.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.723
I was so immune to that life.

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:51.483
It was ridiculous.

00:01:51.483 --> 00:01:53.360
Like, I'm even in it right now,

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.893
still, you know?

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:57.930
It's kind of hard to detach yourself

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:02.810
from something you got so
immune and adapted to, you know?

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:06.930
Rolling with certain age group that,

00:02:09.198 --> 00:02:11.900
you know, it's something that was not

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.587
of a normal type of life, you know?

00:02:14.587 --> 00:02:16.293
- [Interviewer] You left home at what age?

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.427
- Age of 10, 11.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.435
You know what I'm saying?
- Where do you go at 10 or 11?

00:02:23.435 --> 00:02:25.370
I used to always be at my friends' houses.

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:26.853
I never stayed at home.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.260
You know, I would come
home when I wanted to.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:32.280
My mom, she would complain,

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.127
but what can she do?

00:02:34.127 --> 00:02:37.810
You know, I was a adolescence
type of child, you know?

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:39.750
Always wanting to do what I wanna do,

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:41.570
and that's how it's gonna be,

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:45.760
because she showed me that
this is okay, you know?

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.380
So I ran with it,

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:51.410
and decided to do it on my own terms,

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:53.773
and you know, went back home,

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:57.700
and try to make it, you know, work.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:01.280
And there was times that, you know,

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.320
I just didn't like to
bother with my family,

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.283
so leave again.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.970
You know, it's easy to run the streets.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:11.150
Nobody can tell you what to do.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:14.320
You do what you wanna do
and how you wanna do it.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:18.090
My life hasn't been so easy, you know?

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:21.060
But it's good right now.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.370
I'm already immune to, you know?

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.950
Once you get ahold of how you're gonna do

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:26.913
what you wanna do on the streets,

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:30.089
nobody else can tell you anything.

00:03:30.089 --> 00:03:30.922
